# transformers_mtmte_le 0.96 - Spike 3 (64-bit ARM): drafted by s3port.py (PAD-1287) from the Spike 3 port star_wars_elg-1.10.port (star_wars_elg 1.10).
# Functions paired across the two titles: 9883 of 18297 reference functions (8366 anchored by vtable slots and strings, 376 through calls that line up, the rest grown through calls); half of them line up 100% or better.
# Written: what the reference port carries that is the FRAMEWORK's (each site's function at least 75% alike its
# reference's, each global and offset read at the lined-up instruction, the engines' layouts re-read off this program's
# own code); the switch lines from this program's own device table. The reference game's own content (shows, lamps,
# callouts, scenes, held coils, its modes) is not this title's: written as comments, for its own port.
# Emulator-proven 2026-11-16 (PAD-1293) on the Spike 3 rig (tools/spike3_emu/proofs/s3proof.sh TITLE=transformers_mtmte_le,
# slots 160-163, hidden, muted, prebuilt/mode64.so): the runtime took this port whole (30 sites, 37 shots), held back
# the Insider achievement query (type 28) and took its shots from the switch drain's edges (switch_edge). CLOCK TEST (a
# mode file: trigger 0x4 x3, 25 s, shots 0x202000002) started on the third Megatron target left hit, scored 6 shots
# through the game's score_add (+21,000,000: score 275,000 -> 21,477,650) and ended when its 25 s ran out.
# Program sha1 a3b67ca1f27d43de47bb15f73cc2a7808ea36439 (games/game).
# Ball save (PROOF=ballsave): SAVE TEST's 15 s save through multiball_serve, the drain inside it served back (trough
# eject, auto plunger), 3 shots scored on that ball, the drain after the save ended it; the control (no ball_save) ended
# the ball on its first drain. Multiball (PROOF=mb): a mode file's `multiball 3 10` had the game serve 3 balls, ran its
# 40 s clock and gave the game its multiball back at one ball.
# Switch ids are MEASURED (proofs/s3census.sh, proofs/titles/transformers_mtmte_le-0.96.switch_ids): all 37 switch lines
# reached the modes, each 3 below its device-table rank. Not carried: the game's own modes, shows, lamps, callouts,
# screens and held coils (ELG's coil_take / coil_give are its own), for later work.

game           transformers_mtmte_le
version        0.96

